            <ArticleTitle>[Treatment of pilonidal sinus].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2963-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Surgical treatment of pilonidal sinus often leads to significant pain, extended period of wound healing and convalescence, and carries a substantial risk of recurrence. Based on extant surgical evidence, the present review suggests a differential step-up surgical strategy to optimise surgical outcome in the treatment of pilonidal sinus.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
